  "support": "The strongest support for the proposed 400-compound MMV Pathogen Box tachyzoite screen comes from Hayward et al., 2022-02, who screened the same 400-compound Pathogen Box against intact T. gondii in 96-well Seahorse XFe96 format with DMSO negative control and identified 7/400 compounds that reduced O2 consumption, then confirmed activity with fluorescence proliferation assays in T. gondii and P. falciparum, flow cytometry viability, and human cell proliferation assays [(Hayward et al., 2022-02)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/91528e3922fc8dcbae597add91ec748fcfb9f60f). This directly supports the feasibility of using the Pathogen Box, DMSO control, and a phenotypic tachyzoite viability readout, and provides an empirical hit rate (~1.75%) that can inform replicate number and hit selection for the proposed 10 uM, 7-day tdTomato screen. A second, weaker but relevant support is that Hayward et al. identified MMV688853 as an electron transport chain inhibitor in a TgCDPK1-independent manner at the Qi site of Complex III and showed limited cross-resistance in atovaquone-resistant T. gondii and P. falciparum and no cross-resistance in ELQ-300-resistant T. gondii, which supports the plan's emphasis on mitochondrial/ETC targets and comparative analysis with bc1 inhibitors such as atovaquone and buparvaquone. Viewed iteratively, the older Murata et al. 2017-06 framework is extended by Hayward's 2022 Pathogen Box tachyzoite screen, but Hayward does not test the bradyzoite washout endpoint. The weakest support is from Murata et al., 2017-06, whose section headings indicate a phenotypic anti-Toxoplasma compound screen, validation of the parasite growth assay with a pyrimethamine dose-response curve, host cell cytotoxicity testing, and a bradyzoite differentiation assay, and whose reported hits tanshinone IIA and hydroxyzine were described as inhibiting intracellular parasite growth and affecting bradyzoites [(Murata et al., 2017-06)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/837e410f668638b1ac773178019675813e8082c9); this supports the general logic of combining tachyzoite screening, cytotoxicity controls, and bradyzoite-stage assessment, but it does not confirm the proposed Pathogen Box, 10 uM, 7-day, tdTomato, or 28-day washout regrowth conditions.",
  "contradictions": "The strongest contradiction is that neither related work validates the proposed bradyzoite-specific endpoint: the newer Hayward et al. 2022-02 work neither confirms nor refutes the older Murata et al. 2017-06 bradyzoite differentiation claim [(Murata et al., 2017-06)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/837e410f668638b1ac773178019675813e8082c9), but Hayward used intact tachyzoites and oxygen consumption/proliferation readouts and did not include mature bradyzoites, tdTomato-specific fluorescence, or a 28-day inhibitor-washout regrowth assay [(Hayward et al., 2022-02)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/91528e3922fc8dcbae597add91ec748fcfb9f60f), so the central chronic-stage extension of the proposed method remains unsupported by direct evidence. A second contradiction is that Hayward's primary tachyzoite readout was Seahorse XFe96 oxygen consumption rather than tdTomato fluorescence, and the excerpt does not report the exact 10 uM, 7-day treatment, numeric IC50, OCR fold-change, or p-values; therefore the proposed 10 uM, 7-day tdTomato screen is not directly benchmarked against the closest Pathogen Box study and may miss or rank compounds differently if OCR and fluorescence proliferation are not concordant. A third, weaker contradiction is that Murata et al. 2017-06 provides only section headings and no quantitative IC50, LC50, percent inhibition, fold-change, or statistical significance, and does not specify compound concentration, treatment duration, parasite strain, cell line, fluorescence instrument, or washout period [(Murata et al., 2017-06)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/837e410f668638b1ac773178019675813e8082c9); thus it cannot confirm that bradyzoite effects observed in that work would translate to the proposed 28-day regrowth metric. Finally, the related work does not address the proposed metabolomic, LightBBB/SwissADME, MitoTracker, TEM, or ATP-starvation components, so those downstream analyses remain methodologically unvalidated by these sources.",
  "suggested_action": "Most important, add a bradyzoite validation arm that directly tests the proposed 28-day washout regrowth endpoint using the myotube-derived mature bradyzoites, with tdTomato fluorescence quantified at defined time points and a DMSO negative control, because neither Hayward et al. 2022-02 nor Murata et al. 2017-06 provides quantitative evidence for this endpoint [(Hayward et al., 2022-02)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/91528e3922fc8dcbae597add91ec748fcfb9f60f) [(Murata et al., 2017-06)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/837e410f668638b1ac773178019675813e8082c9). Second, incorporate Hayward's tachyzoite readout strategy as a parallel or confirmatory assay: use 96-well Seahorse XFe96 OCR or an equivalent mitochondrial respiration assay alongside tdTomato fluorescence for the 400 Pathogen Box compounds, because Hayward identified 7/400 OCR inhibitors and linked MMV688853 to Complex III, which is directly relevant to the plan's mitochondrial/ETC focus [(Hayward et al., 2022-02)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/91528e3922fc8dcbae597add91ec748fcfb9f60f). Third, specify and report quantitative validation for all hits: serial dilution IC50 for tachyzoites and LC50 for bradyzoites, DMSO controls, replicate number, statistical tests, and cytotoxicity thresholds using resazurin or the human cell proliferation assays used by Hayward, to avoid host-cell toxicity false positives [(Hayward et al., 2022-02)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/91528e3922fc8dcbae597add91ec748fcfb9f60f). Fourth, use the older Murata framework to include a known active control such as pyrimethamine dose-response and a bradyzoite differentiation/cytotoxicity validation, but upgrade it with the proposed tdTomato and 28-day regrowth metrics so that the bradyzoite claim is quantitative rather than inferential [(Murata et al., 2017-06)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/837e410f668638b1ac773178019675813e8082c9). Fifth, for compounds with ETC-like signatures, pe